# `edge a -[has # hash]-> b` stood here as a THIRD error line until
# 0.1. It pinned the exact behaviour 253 contradicted: 253 pins
# `["has # hash"]` as the correct way to write a hash inside a label, this
# case pinned the bare form as `unterminated [label]`. Two deliberate goldens
# encoding opposite answers about one verbatim region. `VERBATIM-REGION-SCOPE` made `[ ]` a
# verbatim region for `#` as it already was for `;`, and the line moved to
# 262-edge-bracket-hash as a MODEL golden.
node a "A"
node b "B"
edge a -[]-> b
edge a -[oops-> b
